From: macOS-Pad-6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tests/test_vm: driver-allocated BOs are exclusive, as UniXNU/Adreno740 d834731

SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause-Patent

The fork's 1c4065c ("map owned and exclusive imported memory without alias scans") maps memory the driver
allocated through the exclusive batch: NativeAdrenoVm::exclusivePages returns true for every non-imported BO,
because such a BO owns its pages until its unmap has completed (the free waits for it), so no other mapping
can alias them in another cache class. tests/test_vm.cpp was not updated: it forces two driver BOs onto the
same physical page (fixture.next_physical) and still expects a different-class map of the second, and of a
scattered BO over the same pages, to be refused with kIOReturnBadArgument. On arm64 the patched fork stopped
there (known-fail of scripts/test_adreno650.py, line 190).

Upstream Adreno740 made the same driver change and replaced these expectations in d834731 (2026-10-28) with
the one below: the different-class map of a driver BO succeeds; imports keep the alias pass, which
test_vm_alias covers. This takes upstream's block unchanged. It changes the test, not the driver: the state
it sets up (two driver BOs on one page) cannot arise from the driver's allocator, and the hazard it would
mean on hardware (one page under two memory attributes) is the allocator's invariant, not checked here.

diff --git a/tests/test_vm.cpp b/tests/test_vm.cpp
index 4dcca86..efca7f4 100644
--- a/tests/test_vm.cpp
+++ b/tests/test_vm.cpp
@@ -185,13 +185,9 @@ int main()
         CHECK(!many.allocate(8192,40,false,8192)&&many.spanCount()==2);fixture.mode=Contiguous;
         uint64_t a=0,b=0;CHECK(!s.vm.map(&first,0,0x800000,3,0,2,&a));
         CHECK(!s.vm.map(&second,0,0x802000,1,0,2,&b));CHECK(!s.vm.unmap(b));
-        const unsigned calls=f.calls;
-        for(unsigned change=0;change<3;++change) {
-            CHECK(s.vm.map(&second,0,0x802000,change==2?9:3,change==0?1:0,change==1?3:2,&b)==kIOReturnBadArgument);
-            CHECK(!b&&!second.deviceReferences()&&f.calls==calls&&!s.vm.poisoned());
-        }
-        CHECK(s.vm.map(&many,0,0x802000,3,1,3,&b)==kIOReturnBadArgument);
-        CHECK(!b&&!many.deviceReferences()&&f.calls==calls&&!s.vm.poisoned());
+        /* Driver-allocated pages are exclusive to their BO (exclusivePages): no cross-class alias pass runs for them, so a different
+         * class over the same pages maps. Imports keep the pass (test_vm_alias covers the index). */
+        CHECK(!s.vm.map(&second,0,0x802000,3,1,2,&b) && !s.vm.unmap(b));
         CHECK(!s.vm.unmap(a)&&!first.release()&&!second.release()&&!many.release());
         CHECK(!s.vm.detach()&&!s.tables.retireAfterQuiescence()&&!s.tables.release());
         CHECK(fixture.live.empty()&&fixture.metadata.empty());
